Subject: CK: fix fwd K/V/bias window offsets for sink + local mask

The learnable-softmax sink (kHasSink) only needs the per-head sink logit; it does
not use CK's StreamingLLM sink column prefix, so TransformerEngine passes
sink_size = 0 and num_sink_loop is therefore 0.

The K, V and bias windows are all built at kv_load_start, which already equals
seqlen_k_start when there is no sink phase. Each kHasSink block then moved its
window by another (seqlen_k_start - sink_seq_end) on the first iteration, so with
a local (sliding-window) mask, where seqlen_k_start > 0, the windows were offset
twice.

In BlockFmhaPipelineQRKSVS this is live for K/V: the loop increments in
`while(++i_total_loops < num_total_loop)`, after the `i_total_loops == 0` check,
so K/V tiles were read from the wrong -- and eventually out-of-range -- offsets.
Forward output was garbage (rel. err ~1.0) for every query tile whose window
starts past column 0. This is what made post-scale-bias + SWA + sink fail while
plain SWA + sink passed: the no-bias config selects the async pipeline, where
the equivalent K/V block sits after the increment and can never fire.

The bias window has the same defect in both pipelines, and randval (dropout)
likewise.

Guard each transition on an actual sink phase, using the
`i_total_loops == num_sink_loop - 1` form the batch_prefill pipeline already
uses: identical behavior when num_sink_loop == 1, inert when it is 0.

Not addressed here: the K/V block in BlockFmhaPipelineQRKSVSAsync is dead code
(the check follows the increment), so the sink prefix jump never happens there.
That only affects sink_size > 0, which TransformerEngine does not use, and it
cannot be validated from here, so it is left alone deliberately.

diff --git a/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/pipeline/block_fmha_pipeline_qr_ks_vs.hpp b/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/pipeline/block_fmha_pipeline_qr_ks_vs.hpp
index 9b932462d..9cd0ddd81 100644
--- a/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/pipeline/block_fmha_pipeline_qr_ks_vs.hpp
+++ b/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/pipeline/block_fmha_pipeline_qr_ks_vs.hpp
@@ -774,7 +774,12 @@ struct BlockFmhaPipelineQRKSVS
             }
             if constexpr(kHasSink)
             {
-                if(i_total_loops == 0)
+                // Only jump out of the sink prefix when a sink phase actually ran.
+                // bias_dram_window already starts at kv_load_start, which equals
+                // seqlen_k_start when sink_seq_end == 0, so an unconditional move here
+                // double-offsets the bias tile for a learnable-softmax sink combined
+                // with a local (sliding-window) mask. Matches the batch_prefill pipeline.
+                if(i_total_loops == num_sink_loop - 1)
                     move_tile_window(bias_dram_window, {0, seqlen_k_start - sink_seq_end});
             }
             move_tile_window(bias_dram_window, {0, kN0});
@@ -946,7 +951,9 @@ struct BlockFmhaPipelineQRKSVS
                         return seqlen_k_start + i_total_loops * kN0;
 
                     const bool in_sink_phase = (num_sink_loop > i_total_loops);
-                    if(i_total_loops == num_sink_loop)
+                    // Same guard as the bias window above: with no sink phase the window
+                    // already starts at seqlen_k_start, so skip the transition move.
+                    if(num_sink_loop > 0 && i_total_loops == num_sink_loop)
                         move_tile_window(randval_dram_window, {0, seqlen_k_start - sink_seq_end});
 
                     return in_sink_phase ? (kv_load_start + i_total_loops * kN0)
@@ -1119,7 +1126,12 @@ struct BlockFmhaPipelineQRKSVS
             // move K tile windows
             if constexpr(kHasSink)
             {
-                if(i_total_loops == 0)
+                // Same guard as the bias window: the K/V windows already start at
+                // kv_load_start, so firing this on the first iteration when no sink
+                // phase ran offsets them a second time by seqlen_k_start. Unlike the
+                // async pipeline (which increments i_total_loops before this check),
+                // here the check is live, so a local mask read wrong K/V tiles.
+                if(i_total_loops == num_sink_loop - 1)
                 {
                     move_tile_window(k_dram_block_window, {seqlen_k_start - sink_seq_end, 0});
                     move_tile_window(v_dram_window, {0, seqlen_k_start - sink_seq_end});
